title: Infoblox: DHCP high availability group
agents: infoblox_csp
catalog: cloud/infoblox
license: GPLv2
distribution: mkp
description:
 Reports the status of a DHCP high availability group, the role and state
 of each member, and the age of the oldest heartbeat across the group.

 Group status and member state mappings are both configurable. Member
 states are Kea high availability state machine values, described further
 in the manual page for the per server high availability check.

 An empty IPv6 status means IPv6 is not configured and is not treated as a
 failure.

discovery:
 One service is created per high availability group in the tenant, on the
 tenant host.

item:
 The group name as configured in the portal.
